+/*
+ * The capture's own bookkeeping, four words of INCAP (0x06940000), reached
+ * through the read-only syscon the capture driver reads its geometry from:
+ *
+ *   +0x104  (frame << 16) | line of the source, as the capture writes it
+ *   +0x8f0  the luma slot table, six words, physical address >> 4; entries
+ *           0..2 are the three ring slots the firmware's pointers rotate over
+ *   +0x930  the chroma table, same shape, same order
+ *   +0xa0c  the index (0..2) of the slot the capture is writing right now
+ *
+ * Measured 11.10.2026 on the HY300 Pro with a moving 1080p60 source scaled to
+ * the 720p panel (arbeit/aufnahme-takt-20261011, zeitleiste2.py, reading the
+ * slots' contents beside the registers): at every source frame boundary the
+ * index steps by one in the order of the table, the capture starts writing
+ * that slot 1.6 ms later, top to bottom, and finishes just before the next
+ * boundary. A, B, C, A, B, C -- no slot is written twice in a row, so a slot
+ * that has just been finished stays whole for two more frame periods.
+ */
